			SPECIAL QUALITIES
	  ====================================
	  ====================================-->
	<special_qualities>
		<!-- Visible All "Special Ability" Ability Objects -->
		<special_quality>
			<name>Armored Casting (Ex)</name>
			<description>You can cast bard spells while wearing light armor and use a shield without incurring the normal arcane spell failure chance.</description>
			<type>BARDCLASSFEATURES.SPECIALQUALITY.EXTRAORDINARY</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect></aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Core Rulebook, p.35</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Bardic Knowledge (Ex)</name>
			<description>You add +2 to all Knowledge checks and may make all Knowledge skill checks untrained.</description>
			<type>BARDCLASSFEATURES.SPECIALQUALITY.EXTRAORDINARY.BARDIC KNOWLEDGE.BARDKNOWLEDGE</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect></aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Core Rulebook, p.35</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Bardic Performance</name>
			<description>You are trained to use the Perform skill to create magical effects on those around you, including yourself if desired. You are trained to use the Perform skill to create magical effects on those around you, including yourself if desired. You can use this ability for 15 rounds per day. Each round, you can produce any one of the types of bardic performance that you have mastered. Starting a bardic performance is a standard action, but it can be maintained each round as a free action. Changing a bardic performance from one effect to another requires the bard to stop the previous performance and start a new one as a standard action. A bardic performance cannot be disrupted, but it ends immediately if you are killed, paralyzed, stunned, knocked unconscious, or otherwise prevented from taking a free action to maintain it each round. You cannot have more than one bardic performance in effect at one time.</description>
			<type>BARDCLASSFEATURES.SPECIALQUALITY.BARDICPERFORMANCE.BARDIC PERFORMANCE</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect>CheckCount: 15, CheckType: Rounds per days, MasterAbility: Bardic Performance</aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Core Rulebook, p.35</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Cantrips</name>
			<description>You have learned a number of cantrips, or 0-level spells. These spells are cast like any other spells, but they do not consume any slots and may be used again.</description>
			<type>BARDCLASSFEATURES.SPECIALQUALITY</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect></aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Core Rulebook, p.38</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Countersong (Su)</name>
			<description>You can counter magic effects that depend on sound (but not spells that have verbal components). Each round of the countersong you make a Perform (keyboard, percussion, wind, string, or sing) skill check. Any creature within 30 feet (including yourself) that is affected by a sonic or language-dependent magical attack may use your Perform check result in place of its saving throw if, after the saving throw is rolled, the Perform check result proves to be higher. If a creature within range of the countersong is already under the effect of a noninstantaneous sonic or language-dependent magical attack, it gains another saving throw against the effect each round it hears the countersong, but it must use your Perform skill check result for the save. Countersong does not work on effects that don&#39;t allow saves. Countersong relies on audible components.</description>
			<type>BARDCLASSFEATURES.SPECIALQUALITY.SUPERNATURAL.BARDICPERFORMANCE.BARDIC PERFORMANCE.BARDCOUNTERSONG</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect>ChildAbility: Bardic Performance</aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Core Rulebook, p.36</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Defensive Training</name>
			<description>Gnomes get a +4 dodge bonus to AC against monsters of the giant subtype.</description>
			<type>RACIALTRAITS.GNOME RACIAL TRAIT.GNOME RACIAL DEFAULT.SPECIALQUALITY.DEFENSIVE.RACIALDEFENSIVETRAINING</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect>Ability Benefit: (+4 dodge bonus to AC vs. giants), CombatBonus: +4 dodge bonus to AC against monsters of the giant subtype.</aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Advanced Race Guide, p.30</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Gnome Magic</name>
			<description>Gnomes add +1 to the DC of any saving throws against illusion spells that they cast. Gnomes with a Charisma of 11 or higher also gain the following spell-like abilities: 1/day--dancing lights, ghost sound, prestidigitation, and speak with animals. The caster level for these effects is equal to the gnome&#39;s level. The DC for these spells is equal to 10 + the spell&#39;s level + the gnome&#39;s Charisma modifier.</description>
			<type>RACIALTRAITS.GNOME RACIAL TRAIT.GNOME RACIAL DEFAULT.SPECIALQUALITY.SPECIAL QUALITY.APPLIED BONUS</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect></aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Advanced Race Guide, p.30</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Illusion Resistance</name>
			<description>Gnomes get a +2 racial saving throw bonus against illusion spells and effects.</description>
			<type>RACIALTRAITS.GNOME RACIAL TRAIT.GNOME RACIAL DEFAULT.SPECIALQUALITY</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect>SaveBonus: +2 racial saving throw bonus against illusion spells and effects.</aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Advanced Race Guide, p.30</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Inspire Competence (Su)</name>
			<description>You can use your performance to help an ally succeed at a task. That ally must be within 30 feet and be able to hear you. The ally gets a +2 competence bonus on skill checks with a particular skill as long as she continues to hear your performance. Certain uses of this ability are infeasible, such as Stealth, and may be disallowed at the GM&#39;s discretion. A bard can&#39;t inspire competence in himself. Inspire competence relies on audible components.</description>
			<type>BARDCLASSFEATURES.SPECIALQUALITY.SUPERNATURAL.BARDICPERFORMANCE.BARDIC PERFORMANCE</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect>ChildAbility: Bardic Performance</aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Core Rulebook, p.37</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Inspire Courage (Su)</name>
			<description>You can use your performance to inspire courage in your allies (including yourself), bolstering them against fear and improving their combat abilities. To be affected, an ally must be able to perceive your performance. An affected ally receives a +1 morale bonus on saving throws against charm and fear effects and a +1 competence bonus on attack and weapon damage rolls. Inspire courage is a mind-affecting ability. Inspire courage can use audible or visual components. The bard must choose which component to use when starting his performance.</description>
			<type>BARDCLASSFEATURES.SPECIALQUALITY.SUPERNATURAL.BARDICPERFORMANCE.BARDIC PERFORMANCE</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect>ChildAbility: Bardic Performance</aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Core Rulebook, p.37</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Keen Senses</name>
			<description>Gnomes receive a +2 racial bonus on Perception skill checks.</description>
			<type>RACIALTRAITS.GNOME RACIAL TRAIT.GNOME RACIAL DEFAULT.SPECIALQUALITY</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect></aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Advanced Race Guide, p.30</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Low-Light Vision (Ex)</name>
			<description>Gnomes can see twice as far as humans in conditions of dim light.</description>
			<type>RACIALTRAITS.GNOME RACIAL TRAIT.GNOME RACIAL DEFAULT.SPECIALQUALITY.EXTRAORDINARY.RACIAL VISION</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect></aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Advanced Race Guide, p.30</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Obsessive</name>
			<description>Gnomes receive a +2 racial bonus on a Craft or Profession skill of their choice.</description>
			<type>RACIALTRAITS.GNOME RACIAL TRAIT.GNOME RACIAL DEFAULT.SPECIALQUALITY</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect></aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Advanced Race Guide, p.30</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Weapon Familiarity</name>
			<description>Gnomes treat any weapon with the word &quot;gnome&quot; in its name as a martial weapon.</description>
			<type>RACIALTRAITS.GNOME RACIAL TRAIT.GNOME RACIAL DEFAULT.SPECIALQUALITY.WEAPON FAMILIARITY.RACIALWEAPONFAMILIARITY</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect></aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
			<virtual>F</virtual>
			<category>Special Ability</category>
			<source>Paizo Inc. - Advanced Race Guide, p.30</source>
		</special_quality>
		<special_quality>
			<name>Well-Versed (Ex)</name>
			<description>You have becomes resistant to the Bardic Performance of others, and to sonic effects in general. You gain a +4 bonus on saving throws made against Bardic Performance, sonic, and language-dependent effects.</description>
			<type>BARDCLASSFEATURES.SPECIALQUALITY.EXTRAORDINARY.BARDWELLVERSED</type>
			<associated></associated>
			<count>0</count>
			<aspect>SaveBonus: +4 vs. Bardic Performance, sonic, and language-dependent effects</aspect>
			<auto>F</auto>
			<hidden>F</hidden>
